  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-21T07:34:43.211Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I set a PhysBone component on a bone within the humanoid rig, Multi Child Type as Ignored and IsAnimated to true. Grab feature is on.\n\nThis seems to be a good workaround for humanoid bones to work as root transforms to reduce duplicate components (ears for example). But there are a few issues with it:\n\n- The root bone seems to not be grabbable whatsoever, which is a good thing for my case.\n\n- When I grab a child bone, the root bone stops being tracked until released. For example, in VR, when I move my head around while grabbing an ear, the head of my avatar stays in place.\n\n- On a side note, having to set the humanoid bone as animated no matter if its child bones are animated or not could create performance issues.\n\nCould you make an option so that the root bone can be fully ignored by any transformation and interaction from the PhysBone component?\n\n(Edit: added more details and changed suggestion)",
